==Faroese==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{term|vinna|lang=non}}.

====Noun====
{{fo-noun|f|vinnu|vinnur}}

# [[business]], [[acquisition]], [[work]], [[profession]]
# {{context|lang=fo|archaic|agriculture}} [[ploughing]]

=====Declension=====
{{fo-decl-noun-f1|vinn}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{term|vinna|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{recons|winnaną|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{recons|wen-||to strive, wish, desire, love|lang=ine-pro}}. Related to Icelandic and Swedish {{term|vinna|lang=is}}, Norwegian {{term|vinne|lang=no}}, English {{term|win||lang=en}}, Dutch {{term|winnen|lang=nl}}, and German {{term|gewinnen||lang=de}}.

====Verb====
{{fo-verb|vann|vunnu|vunnið}}

# to [[win]]
# to [[earn]]
# to [[get]]
# to [[work]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{fo-conj-44|v|i|n|u|a}}

