==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvɪnːa/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ɪnːa|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|vinna|lang=non}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|f|vinnu|-}}

# a [[job]], an [[occupation]], an [[employment]]{{jump|is|employment|s}}
#: ''Að [[hafa vinnu|hafa '''vinnu''']].''
#:: To be '''employed'''.
# [[work]], [[labour]]{{jump|is|labour|s}}

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-f-w1|v|i|nn|pl=-}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|hafa vinnu}}
* {{l|is|heimavinna}}
* {{l|is|erfiðisvinna}}
* {{l|is|vinnuhlé}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{jump|s|is|employment}} {{l|is|atvinna}}
* {{jump|s|is|labour}} {{l|is|verk}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|vinna|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|winnaną|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|wen-||to strive, wish, desire, love|lang=ine-pro}}. Related to Faroese and Swedish {{term|vinna|lang=is}}, Norwegian {{term|vinne|lang=no}}, English {{term|win||lang=en}}, Dutch {{term|winnen|lang=nl}}, and German {{term|gewinnen||lang=de}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-strong|vann|unnu|unnið}}

# to [[work]]
#: ''Ég nenni ekki að '''vinna'''.''
#:: I don't want to '''work'''.
#: ''Ég '''vinn''' allan daginn.''
#:: I '''work''' all day.
# to [[win]]
#: ''Við '''unnum'''!''
#:: We '''won'''!
#: ''Ég '''vann'''!''
#:: I '''won'''!

