==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{recons|winnaną|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{recons|wen-||to strive, wish, desire, love|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Old English {{term|winnan|lang=ang}}, Old Saxon {{term|winnan|lang=osx}}, Old High German ''winnan'', Gothic {{term|𐍅𐌹𐌽𐌽𐌰𐌽|tr=winnan|lang=got}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb|vann|unnu|unnit}}

# to [[accomplish]]

====Synonyms====
* {{l|non|fremja}}
* {{l|non|inna}}

====Descendants====
* Faroese: {{l|fo|vinna}}
* Icelandic: {{l|is|vinna}}
* Norwegian: {{l|no|vinne}}
* Swedish: {{l|sv|vinna}}

